WEBVTT

00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:04.336
Journey twenty-six: download data and delete account.

00:00:04.336 --> 00:00:08.856
New in this run: a download that could not be prepared says so, a

00:00:08.856 --> 00:00:13.446
deletion stays deleted after a backup is restored, and nothing the

00:00:13.446 --> 00:00:15.602
member saw stays on the device.

00:00:16.481 --> 00:00:20.821
When Jubilee could not put the file together after five tries, the

00:00:20.821 --> 00:00:25.423
account page says: We couldn't prepare your data, and the Jubilee team

00:00:25.423 --> 00:00:30.092
has been told. Asking again starts a new download, and the link arrives

00:00:30.092 --> 00:00:32.393
by e-mail within twenty-four hours.

00:00:33.097 --> 00:00:37.979
Delete account opens the dialog with Keep my account in focus, the safe

00:00:37.979 --> 00:00:42.793
choice. It names the account and counts what is deleted and cancelled.

00:00:43.497 --> 00:00:48.537
If the connection drops, nothing was sent, and what was typed is still

00:00:48.537 --> 00:00:48.897
here.

00:00:49.598 --> 00:00:53.054
With the connection back, the account is deleted.

00:00:53.054 --> 00:00:57.919
Jubilee opens the welcome page, and the saved pages, waiting messages

00:00:57.919 --> 00:00:59.894
and drafts leave the device.

00:01:00.767 --> 00:01:05.066
The tests prove the rest: the deletion ledger keeps a deleted account

00:01:05.066 --> 00:01:09.551
deleted after a restore, the archive lives outside the database, and the

00:01:09.551 --> 00:01:12.479
two e-mails are sent whatever the settings say.

00:01:13.347 --> 00:01:18.653
What is left is the owner's: keep the database's backups for thirty-five

00:01:18.653 --> 00:01:19.611
days or less.
